e Oregon Ducks 2012 football schedule?\n", "asr_s": 0.61, "expert_s": 5.79, "expert_input_samples": 49022, "expert_input_s": 3.064, "expert_input_sha256": "bbbf981b7614aa7cafb7a7f17c9197226fccf1545cba79187e873f834166a08b", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 5.759, "relay_synth_ms": 4935, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 41, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 41, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0113_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "134d333861f00807c6935e81b10ba0d42118d22d14df464b949e277a18a3f23b", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 10.36}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0113_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "48ffc6db410b68bc685208ae435e5011d8729a65c7421c6ab24b6cf2f26818ef", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0113_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "d9c069d4c42653dbf81f80e83d46016c712cd13eb95f4a90eef1e3d787433332", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.056, 1.101, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.064, 2.115, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.059, 3.105, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 3.064, 3.162, 3.568, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 3.064, "last_real_feed_done": 3.162, "onset": 3.568, "gate_read_done": 3.568, "fire": 3.568, "candidate_first_pcm": 3.568, "stall_note": 3.569, "stall_first_pcm": 4.215, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 4.215, "expert_req": 3.569, "expert_resp": 9.974, "relay_synth_start": 9.975, "relay_first_pcm": 10.604, "relay_synth_end": 14.91, "first_any_pcm": 3.568, "first_answer_pcm": 10.604, "session_end": 15.026}, "ttfa_answer_s": 7.54, "ttfa_any_s": 0.504}
{"id": "swebq0121", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2104713991, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "aa7a8a6f2040793a4fe8dabcb6d10f2520887b0e0988d37809c3a27ef31575d8", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "what type of religion did massachusetts have?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0121.wav", "input_sha256": "371831f391fc193eabea55156e64d6a4054fec73cf9aed24af8cd650e1e3b7a7", "input_samples": 42335, "input_s": 2.646, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.9172, "act": 0.9982, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "Massachusetts had a Puritan religion — a strict form of Protestant Christianity. In colonial Massachusetts, the Puritan church was closely tied to the government.", "expert_answer": "Massachusetts had a **Puritan** religion — a strict form of **Protestant Christianity**. In colonial Massachusetts, the Puritan church was closely tied to the government.", "transcript": "What type of religion did Massachusetts have?\n", "asr_s": 0.6, "expert_s": 1.77, "expert_input_samples": 42335, "expert_input_s": 2.646, "expert_input_sha256": "371831f391fc193eabea55156e64d6a4054fec73cf9aed24af8cd650e1e3b7a7", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 1.525, "relay_synth_ms": 4520, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 66, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 66, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0121_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "9d903be41e4d2f076fff7a8c5486cfcc5efcc6b0dbe972ec97eecee4c5dbb3de", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 10.36}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0121_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "89f74bd2fc20a209e8fbaab5bee8da39aa29cf9e28ddf64c66fd52b27e8c8d17", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0121_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "24fb87e847dfbe2199b3fe4efca9455aef70f0e3714bd9807ddfade48a1cd63c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.6}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.062, 1.113, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.059, 2.113, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.646, 2.704, 2.749, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.646, 3.704, 4.244, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.646, 4.77, 5.082, 0, 14400, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.646, "last_real_feed_done": 2.704, "onset": 4.244, "gate_read_done": 4.244, "fire": 4.244, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.244, "stall_note": 4.245, "stall_first_pcm": 4.713, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 5.082, "expert_req": 4.245, "expert_resp": 6.606, "relay_synth_start": 6.607, "relay_first_pcm": 7.238, "relay_synth_end": 11.127, "first_any_pcm": 4.244, "first_answer_pcm": 7.238, "session_end": 11.4}, "ttfa_answer_s": 4.592, "ttfa_any_s": 1.598}
{"id": "swebq0130", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 326066896, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "aa7a8a6f2040793a4fe8dabcb6d10f2520887b0e0988d37809c3a27ef31575d8", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "what is jimi hendrix purple haze about?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0130.wav", "input_sha256": "0e91c91dbc19d305a2c1035c510f92aa3e84e4b9003c60b9b6e27fef6f19af6e", "input_samples": 34162, "input_s": 2.135, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.5538, "act": 0.9984, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "“Purple Haze” is mainly about a disorienting, overwhelming state of mind—confusion, desire, and altered perception. Jimi Hendrix often said the song was inspired by a dream and science-fiction imagery, not simply drugs. So, in short: it’s about feeling caught in a surreal, intoxicating mental haze, with love and psychedelic imagery mixed together.", "expert_answer": "“**Purple Haze**” is mainly about a **disorienting, overwhelming state of mind**—confusion, desire, and altered perception.\n\nJimi Hendrix often said the song was inspired by a **dream** and science-fiction imagery, not simply drugs. The lyrics describe someone who feels mentally and emotionally “fogged,” unsure whether what he’s experiencing is love, madness, or some strange spell: “Am I happy or in misery?” The “purple haze” works as a metaphor for being consumed by sensation—possibly romantic obsession, psychedelic experience, or general confusion.\n\nSo, in short: **it’s about feeling caught in a surreal, intoxicating mental haze, with love and psychedelic imagery mixed together.**", "transcript": "What is Jimi Hendrix Purple Haze about?\n", "asr_s": 0.57, "expert_s": 4.51, "expert_input_samples": 34162, "expert_input_s": 2.135, "expert_input_sha256": "0e91c91dbc19d305a2c1035c510f92aa3e84e4b9003c60b9b6e27fef6f19af6e", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 3.835, "relay_synth_ms": 9829, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 1, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0130_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "52ee550abe79d2350d5ea30b6d6e6a5b61f725032bdc1f379063b3cefa81a26c", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 21.88}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0130_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "6835e921a2410e6355ecf586370f930ec4eec10b80a679f7ad2e5baef0c6d3b1", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0130_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "53e7296086a923edcf2de622b759b022bce9afd1cd3f384cc5ba8fe5edcc5ca3", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 2.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.055, 1.099, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.057, 2.103, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 2.135, 2.191, 2.235, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.135, 3.193, 3.535, 0, 24000, 0], [4, 0, 4.135, 4.194, 4.78, 0, 30720, 1]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 2.135, "last_real_feed_done": 2.191, "onset": 3.535, "gate_read_done": 3.535, "fire": 3.535, "candidate_first_pcm": 3.535, "stall_note": 3.535, "stall_first_pcm": 4.003, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 4.78, "expert_req": 3.535, "expert_resp": 8.614, "relay_synth_start": 8.615, "relay_first_pcm": 9.235, "relay_synth_end": 18.445, "first_any_pcm": 3.535, "first_answer_pcm": 9.235, "session_end": 18.596}, "ttfa_answer_s": 7.1, "ttfa_any_s": 1.4}
{"id": "swebq0139", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 1790171764, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "aa7a8a6f2040793a4fe8dabcb6d10f2520887b0e0988d37809c3a27ef31575d8", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "what to do san jose ca?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0139.wav", "input_sha256": "278df973e7100f9c49e8bfc50f45206ee24e6e26dee3d9bd2f9fca3aa231fe4f", "input_samples": 25988, "input_s": 1.624, "n_real_chunks": 2, "score": 0.9237, "act": 0.9918, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "It looks like “Watashi sanaseka” may be a typo or romanized Japanese attempt. , Watashi = “I” / “me” in Japanese. , sanaseka doesn’t appear to be standard Japanese. Did you mean something like: Watashi wa ... = “I am ...” , Watashi wa Sanaseka desu = “I am Sanaseka” / “My name is Sanaseka” , Watashi wa genki desu = “I am fine” If you tell me what you meant to say, I can translate or correct it.", "expert_answer": "It looks like **“Watashi sanaseka”** may be a typo or romanized Japanese attempt.\n\n- **Watashi** = “I” / “me” in Japanese.\n- **sanaseka** doesn’t appear to be standard Japanese.\n\nDid you mean something like:\n\n- **Watashi wa ...** = “I am ...”\n- **Watashi wa Sanaseka desu** = “I am Sanaseka” / “My name is Sanaseka”\n- **Watashi wa genki desu** = “I am fine”\n\nIf you tell me what you meant to say, I can translate or correct it.", "transcript": "Watashi sanaseka.\n", "asr_s": 0.48, "expert_s": 4.55, "expert_input_samples": 25988, "expert_input_s": 1.624, "expert_input_sha256": "278df973e7100f9c49e8bfc50f45206ee24e6e26dee3d9bd2f9fca3aa231fe4f", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 4.414, "relay_synth_ms": 21118, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0139_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "c0d8757931d8b1d459bee11758273ec1a04c0126c2916194968429b6b8706320", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 50.68}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0139_always_candidate.wav", "sha256": "00b3c06c814e74be25359266c46c39667bf243319b4d49d203fb6ca6ba71d52b", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0139_always_stall.wav", "sha256": "8d938889cd96eec9bb008a8a287a0e89054f933c526a15fe69ce586791752506", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.057, 1.102, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 1.624, 1.682, 1.728, 1, 0, 0], [2, 0, 2.624, 2.681, 2.727, 1, 0, 0], [3, 0, 3.624, 3.682, 4.091, 0, 24000, 0]], "status": "completed", "error": null, "ts": {"feed_start": 0.0, "input_end": 1.624, "last_real_feed_done": 1.682, "onset": 4.091, "gate_read_done": 4.091, "fire": 4.091, "candidate_first_pcm": 4.091, "stall_note": 4.092, "stall_first_pcm": 4.701, "local_first_pcm": null, "wait_start": 4.701, "expert_req": 4.092, "expert_resp": 9.115, "relay_synth_start": 9.116, "relay_first_pcm": 9.752, "relay_synth_end": 30.235, "first_any_pcm": 4.091, "first_answer_pcm": 9.752, "session_end": 30.417}, "ttfa_answer_s": 8.127, "ttfa_any_s": 2.467}
{"id": "swebq0147", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "always", "tier": "always", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3259654580, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "aa7a8a6f2040793a4fe8dabcb6d10f2520887b0e0988d37809c3a27ef31575d8", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "who will be the red sox next coach?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0147.wav", "input_sha256": "14689c9b6682dcfb9aa153f224a904857589a3d0baebea8bd80f05104f6a5941", "input_samples": 34905, "input_s": 2.182, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.8654, "act": 0.9929, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "The Red Sox’s current interim manager is Chad Tracy. Boston parted ways with Alex Cora on April 25, 2026, and named Tracy interim manager. (mlb.com) If you mean the next permanent manager, the team has not officially named one yet based on current reports.", "expert_answer": "The Red Sox’s **current interim manager is Chad Tracy**. Boston parted ways with **Alex Cora** on **April 25, 2026**, and named Tracy interim manager. ([mlb.com](https://www.mlb.com/press-release/red-sox-part-ways-with-alex-cora-and-members-of-the-coaching-staff?utm_source=openai))\n\nIf you mean the **next permanent manager**, the team has **not officially named one yet** based on current reports.", "transcript": "Who will be the Red Sox next coach?\n", "asr_s": 0.7, "expert_s": 6.3, "expert_input_samples": 34905, "expert_input_s": 2.182, "expert_input_sha256": "14689c9b6682dcfb9aa153f224a904857589a3d0baebea8bd80f05104f6a5941", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 6.395, "relay_synth_ms": 7389, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0147_always_relay.wav", "sha256": "9b7524eb4652f5775b61e923ee93edd341a2